# ─── personal data ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The real show history stays off GitHub. Both of these are needed to run the
# site but neither is public: source.csv is the export from the sheet, and
# data.json is built from it and carries exactly the same facts, so ignoring one
# without the other would be pointless.
#
# `data/sample.csv` and `data/sample.overrides.json` are committed in their
# place — the build falls back to them automatically, so a fresh clone runs.
data/source.csv
data/overrides.json
assets/data.json

# Generated from the real data every build: open questions about the private
# history, so it doesn't belong here either.
REVIEW.md

